Expected elements: present

Every MUST SHOW item is there: the affirmative `Real Aztec testnet data` banner above the identity bar naming `aztec-testnet`, its endpoint, moment and 63629–63678 window; an identity bar with a real hash, `block 63675`, both stepping directions, `128 / 345` and the phase rail; an exit that lands on the chain; instruction-level explanations in their own words in Code, Call Trace and Values; `Supply sources`; and replay telemetry with `effectsMismatched: 0`. No invented source, no `aztec` slug, no fixture content, no unexplained blank pane, no failure banner. No dangling separator in the cost row and no language tag on the identity bar.

Typographically the page is clean and the mono texture is right, but the type scale carries almost no hierarchy where it matters most.

Worst: the COST · TRANSACTIONFEE value is a 66-character raw hex quantity set unwrapped-but-wrapping across three right-aligned lines, turning a one-line label/value row into a four-line block whose only significant digits land last. Second: in the same pane, section headings (EXECUTIONS, DECODED INPUT) are typographically identical to field labels (BLOCK, SELECTOR, RAW), so the pane reads as one flat list of eleven labels. Third: the banner's five-line paragraph is the largest run of text on the page, outweighing the session's own identity.

Highest-priority fixes: format or middle-truncate the fee like every other quantity, and introduce one weight or size step between section headings and field labels in the Transaction pane.

Rating: 6/10

